      <h2>Creator income is complex. Generic bookkeeping doesn't cut it.</h2>
      <p>Most bookkeepers are built for businesses that issue invoices and receive checks. YouTube businesses don't work that way. You might receive 12 different AdSense deposits in a year, five brand deal wire transfers, a stream of affiliate commissions, and a Stripe payout from digital products — all in the same month.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;">Categorizing that correctly, reconciling it against your bank accounts, and generating reports that actually make tax time easier requires someone who knows both bookkeeping and the YouTube business model. That's what I provide.</p>
