{# ── FAQ ── #}
<section class="bg-cloud">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:720px;">
    <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
    <h2>Common questions about bookkeeping for YouTubers</h2>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do I really need bookkeeping if I'm just starting out?</summary>
      <p>If your channel is generating any income at all, tracking it from the beginning is much easier than reconstructing a year's worth of transactions at tax time. Starting with clean books — even simple ones — saves money and stress down the line.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What's the difference between bookkeeping and tax prep?</summary>
      <p>Bookkeeping is the ongoing process of recording, categorizing, and reconciling your income and expenses throughout the year. Tax prep uses those records to complete and file your tax return. The two work together — clean books make tax prep faster, cheaper, and more accurate.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do I need to issue 1099s to people I pay for editing or thumbnails?</summary>
      <p>Yes — if you pay a freelance contractor $600 or more in a calendar year, you're required to issue them a 1099-NEC by January 31 of the following year. This includes video editors, thumbnail designers, scriptwriters, and anyone else you pay who isn't an employee. Failing to file can result in IRS penalties.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can you help me catch up on bookkeeping I've been ignoring?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Bookkeeping catch-up is common and very solvable. I'll work through your bank statements, payment processor records, and invoices to reconstruct your books from whenever you need them caught up to.</p>
    </details>

